.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/

# large / regenerable artifacts
models/
data/
vectors/

# results/ is NOT ignored. It was, on the grounds that it is regenerable -- but
# the sweeps in it are hours of GPU on one specific machine, and they are the
# evidence behind every number in report.md and the paper. Regenerating them is
# not the same as having them. Total is 16 MB.
#
# Keep it that way: if something genuinely large and genuinely cheap to rebuild
# lands in results/, ignore that file by name rather than the directory.
#
# eval_gemma_passages.jsonl.decay.jsonl and eval_gemma_passages_decayg.jsonl.decay.jsonl
# (1.4 MB together) are per-token decay traces for the abandoned arm in fail.md
# section 9. The code that produced them is deleted, so they cannot be
# regenerated -- they stay tracked here despite the size, on purpose.
*.safetensors
*.aria2

# paper/ is the write-up. steering.tex and related-work.md are source and
# tracked; everything else there is latex build output or an orphan from an
# earlier draft, ignored by name rather than ignoring paper/ wholesale.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.pdf
paper/*Notes.bib
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.fls
paper/pbcopy
paper/images/pg-*.png
